lity Group"}],"related":"[{\"name\": \"TVS SCS Global Freight Solutions Limited\", \"relation\": \"subsidiary\", \"note\": \"Material unlisted subsidiary; wholly owned subsidiary being merged into TVS Supply Chain Solutions Limited under the Scheme of Amalgamation (application filed with NCLT Chennai)\"}, {\"name\": \"TVS SCS IFM Limited …","risks":[{"note":"Rapid turnover in key managerial personnel — CEO appointed Jan 22, 2026, Managing Director Ravi Viswanathan resigned effective June 30, 2026, and Vikas Chadha appointed MD effective July 1, 2026 — creates continuity and execution risk at the helm of the business.","risk":"Senior leadership churn at the top"},{"note":"Growth is anchored to a relatively small base of large, sophisticated clients (100 Fortune 500 customers serviced, up from 91), and individual strategic contract wins (Global Wind Turbine maker, European retail chain, North America agri-equipment maker); loss or scaling-down of a major account would be material.","risk":"Customer concentration on marquee accounts"},{"note":"The asset-light, tech-led model relies on winning fresh contracts each year to sustain the topline (FY26 added ~Rs 1,206.74 crores of new-business revenue); a slowdown in wins directly compresses growth.","risk":"Dependence on continuous new business development"},{"note":"The consolidated group operates through a large web of international subsidiaries across the UK, USA, Germany, Spain, Singapore, Thailand, Korea, Malaysia, Vietnam, Mexico, Indonesia and others, exposing it to currency, cross-border regulatory and geopolitical risk even though standalone exports are Nil.","risk":"Extensive foreign operations and FX / geopolitical exposure"},{"note":"The segment structure was reorganised during FY26 to merge ISCS and IFM (formerly Rico Logistics) into a single unified ISCS model; combining acquired/foreign entities and re-bundling service lines carries integration and execution risk.","risk":"Integration and restructuring execution risk"},{"note":"Profitability leans on cost-optimisation initiatives and operating leverage from new wins rather than owned assets, leaving margins sensitive to input costs, contract pricing and utilisation swings.","risk":"Margin volatility in the asset-light logistics model"},{"note":"Demand is spread across Automotive, FMCG/FMCD, Electronics, E-commerce, Telecom & IT, Oil & Gas, Cement, Retail, Engineering & Capital Goods, Renewable Energy and Healthcare — a downturn in one or more of these cyclical industries flows through to supply-chain volumes.","risk":"Cyclicality across served end-markets"}],"rpt":{},"rpt_date":"","s":"TVSSCS","sector":"Services","sk":{"as_of":"2026-08-05","cagrs":[{"cagr":"31-32%","period":"CY2025-CY2030P","segment":"Total market opportunity for new age end-to-end horizontal e-commerce enablement platforms (GMV)"},{"cagr":"40-45%","period":"CY2025-CY2030P","segment":"In-store (hyperlocal fulfilment) segment of the addressable opportunity"},{"cagr":"40-50%","period":"CY2025-CY2030P","segment":"Digitally enabled social commerce segment of the addressable opportunity"},{"cagr":"20-25%","period":"CY2025-CY2030P","segment":"Direct commerce"},{"cagr":"14-18%","period":"CY2025-CY2030P","segment":"Other marketplaces (under US$1 billion GMV, no captive logistics)"},{"cagr":"14-20%","period":"CY2025-CY2030P","segment":"Cross-border MSME exports in key categories"},{"cagr":"8-10%","period":"CY2025-CY2030P","segment":"India domestic retail GMV"},{"cagr":"20-25%","period":"CY2025-CY2030P","segment":"India online domestic retail GMV"},{"cagr":"17-22%","period":"CY2025-CY2030P","segment":"Organised retail (brick-and-mortar plus online)"},{"cagr":"16-20%","period":"CY2025-CY2030P","segment":"Organised brick-and-mortar retail"},{"cagr":"5-6%","period":"CY2025-CY2030P","segment":"Unorganised retail"},{"cagr":"22-26%","period":"CY2025-CY2030P","segment":"New age online-first sellers (share of retail GMV)"},{"cagr":"5-7%","period":"CY2025-CY2030P","segmen